message: "If you use this code, please cite it as below and cite the NOMAD dataset."
title: "Project Halide: code for DFT validation of predicted Li/Na metal-halide structures"
type: software
version: "v2.0.1"
date-released: "2026-10-22"
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: Suravarjjala
    given-names: Nikhilesh
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-7227-2213"
    affiliation: "Independent researcher"
  - family-names: Kakani
    given-names: Arnav
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-6170-8342"
    affiliation: "Independent researcher"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23481926"
abstract: >-
  Scripts used to screen, relax and judge predicted (not synthesised) Li/Na
  tetrahalide structure models with MACE-MPA-0 and Quantum ESPRESSO PBE-D3.
  Contains the gate logic (verdict.py), the structure-transplant scan, DFT job
  generators and runner, and the cluster packet workflow. The two headline
  proposed models are TP-NaSbBr4-01 and TP-LiSbBr4-01. All structures are
  predicted or proposed models; no electrolyte is claimed. Raw DFT outputs are
  in the NOMAD datasets, not here.
keywords: [DFT, Quantum ESPRESSO, MACE, metal halides, structure prediction, sodium, lithium]
references:
  - type: dataset
    title: "Independent PBE and PBE-D3 validation (v1)"
    doi: "10.17172/nomad.7c09-m7v2"
